WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.900 --> 00:00:06.317
A basis of a space is a set of vectors

2
00:00:06.406 --> 00:00:08.834
that does two jobs at once

3
00:00:08.834 --> 00:00:12.700
it is independent, and it spans the space.

4
00:00:13.050 --> 00:00:15.444
Back on the drone's plane

5
00:00:15.444 --> 00:00:18.298
laid flat in steps of u and v.

6
00:00:18.298 --> 00:00:20.231
u and v are a basis

7
00:00:20.231 --> 00:00:23.361
their cell tiles the whole plane.

8
00:00:23.361 --> 00:00:26.031
So are u and s, and w and s.

9
00:00:26.123 --> 00:00:28.333
Every pair of buttons is

10
00:00:28.425 --> 00:00:30.450
a basis of this plane.

11
00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:32.336
Two near misses.

12
00:00:32.336 --> 00:00:34.928
u, v and w span the plane

13
00:00:34.928 --> 00:00:38.576
but they are dependent: one too many.

14
00:00:38.576 --> 00:00:42.416
u, v and one, one, one are independent

15
00:00:42.416 --> 00:00:46.160
but one, one, one is not in the plane

16
00:00:46.160 --> 00:00:49.232
so they are a basis of R three

17
00:00:49.232 --> 00:00:50.960
not of the plane.

18
00:00:51.540 --> 00:00:52.443
In a basis

19
00:00:52.525 --> 00:00:55.971
every vector of the space is a combination

20
00:00:56.053 --> 00:00:57.776
of the basis vectors

21
00:00:57.776 --> 00:01:00.812
and the amounts are its coordinates.

22
00:01:00.812 --> 00:01:04.340
Take the delivery point, two, five, three.

23
00:01:04.690 --> 00:01:09.260
In the basis u, v: one u, then one v.

24
00:01:09.260 --> 00:01:11.977
Coordinates one, one.

25
00:01:11.977 --> 00:01:16.671
In the basis u, s: one u, a second u

26
00:01:16.671 --> 00:01:18.153
then one s.

27
00:01:18.153 --> 00:01:20.870
Coordinates two, one.

28
00:01:20.870 --> 00:01:26.181
Check: two times one, two, one, plus zero

29
00:01:26.181 --> 00:01:30.010
one, one, is two, five, three.

30
00:01:30.360 --> 00:01:33.954
In the basis w, s: two thirds of w

31
00:01:33.954 --> 00:01:36.110
then one third of s.

32
00:01:36.110 --> 00:01:37.445
Three bases

33
00:01:37.445 --> 00:01:40.936
three different pairs of numbers

34
00:01:40.936 --> 00:01:43.400
one and the same point.

35
00:01:43.980 --> 00:01:47.387
Could the delivery point have two different

36
00:01:47.466 --> 00:01:50.953
pairs of coordinates in the same basis u, v?

37
00:01:50.953 --> 00:01:52.300
Pause and think.

38
00:01:52.850 --> 00:01:56.792
Suppose a u plus b v and a prime u plus

39
00:01:56.893 --> 00:01:59.825
b prime v are the same point.

40
00:01:59.825 --> 00:02:03.363
Subtract: a minus a prime times u

41
00:02:03.363 --> 00:02:07.305
plus b minus b prime times v, is zero.

42
00:02:07.305 --> 00:02:09.832
u and v are independent

43
00:02:09.832 --> 00:02:12.461
so both amounts are zero

44
00:02:12.461 --> 00:02:15.392
the two pairs were the same.

45
00:02:15.392 --> 00:02:18.930
Coordinates in a basis are unique.

46
00:02:22.510 --> 00:02:25.288
Every basis we found for the drone's

47
00:02:25.365 --> 00:02:27.063
plane had two vectors.

48
00:02:27.063 --> 00:02:28.684
That is no accident

49
00:02:28.684 --> 00:02:31.848
all bases of a space have the same size

50
00:02:31.848 --> 00:02:34.471
and that number is its dimension.

51
00:02:34.549 --> 00:02:36.632
The dimension of the column

52
00:02:36.709 --> 00:02:38.870
space is the rank: here two.

53
00:02:39.220 --> 00:02:42.022
The nullspace lives in R four.

54
00:02:42.022 --> 00:02:45.758
Its basis is the two special solutions

55
00:02:45.758 --> 00:02:49.681
minus two, minus one, one, zero, and one

56
00:02:49.681 --> 00:02:51.736
minus one, zero, one

57
00:02:51.736 --> 00:02:54.632
so its dimension is n minus r

58
00:02:54.632 --> 00:02:57.060
four minus two, also two.

59
00:02:57.410 --> 00:02:58.972
Careful with words

60
00:02:58.972 --> 00:03:02.426
three by four is the shape of the matrix.

61
00:03:02.426 --> 00:03:04.810
Dimensions belong to spaces.

62
00:03:05.390 --> 00:03:07.931
Which columns give a basis

63
00:03:08.029 --> 00:03:09.983
of the column space?

64
00:03:10.081 --> 00:03:13.110
Elimination says the pivots are

65
00:03:13.208 --> 00:03:15.456
in columns one and two.

66
00:03:15.456 --> 00:03:19.169
The pivot columns of R are one, zero

67
00:03:19.169 --> 00:03:21.710
zero and zero, one, zero.

68
00:03:22.060 --> 00:03:25.462
But they are not even in the drone's plane

69
00:03:25.462 --> 00:03:28.072
one minus zero plus zero is one

70
00:03:28.072 --> 00:03:31.474
and zero minus one plus zero is minus one.

71
00:03:31.474 --> 00:03:34.480
Elimination changed the column space.

72
00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:37.487
Take the pivot columns from A itself

73
00:03:37.487 --> 00:03:40.730
u and v: one minus two plus one is zero

74
00:03:40.730 --> 00:03:43.420
one minus three plus two is zero.

75
00:03:44.000 --> 00:03:46.130
A café records six days of

76
00:03:46.211 --> 00:03:48.013
sales and the weather.

77
00:03:48.013 --> 00:03:51.535
The model has an intercept column of ones

78
00:03:51.535 --> 00:03:54.730
and one column each for sunny, cloudy

79
00:03:54.730 --> 00:03:56.040
and rainy days.

80
00:03:56.390 --> 00:04:00.330
Every day is exactly one kind of weather

81
00:04:00.426 --> 00:04:03.405
so sunny plus cloudy plus rainy

82
00:04:03.501 --> 00:04:05.519
equals the intercept.

83
00:04:05.519 --> 00:04:08.882
X times one, minus one, minus one

84
00:04:08.882 --> 00:04:12.246
minus one is zero in all six rows.

85
00:04:12.246 --> 00:04:15.801
Four columns, rank three: dependent

86
00:04:15.897 --> 00:04:18.588
and the model's coefficients

87
00:04:18.684 --> 00:04:20.510
are not determined.

88
00:04:20.860 --> 00:04:24.054
The fix: drop one category, say sunny

89
00:04:24.054 --> 00:04:26.407
which becomes the baseline.

90
00:04:26.407 --> 00:04:29.517
Now rank three equals three columns

91
00:04:29.517 --> 00:04:30.609
independent.

92
00:04:30.609 --> 00:04:32.122
One more warning

93
00:04:32.206 --> 00:04:36.240
two columns that differ by only ten to the minus

94
00:04:36.324 --> 00:04:39.518
thirteen count as rank two by default

95
00:04:39.602 --> 00:04:42.039
and rank one with a tolerance

96
00:04:42.123 --> 00:04:44.140
of ten to the minus six.

97
00:04:44.720 --> 00:04:48.103
So: a basis is independent and spans.

98
00:04:48.194 --> 00:04:50.754
Every vector has exactly one

99
00:04:50.846 --> 00:04:53.131
set of coordinates in it

100
00:04:53.131 --> 00:04:56.789
the delivery point is one, one in u, v

101
00:04:56.789 --> 00:04:58.800
and two, one in u, s.

102
00:04:59.150 --> 00:05:02.789
Every basis of a space has the same size

103
00:05:02.789 --> 00:05:04.120
its dimension

104
00:05:04.120 --> 00:05:06.872
the rank for the column space

105
00:05:06.872 --> 00:05:09.446
n minus r for the nullspace.

106
00:05:09.446 --> 00:05:13.085
Your turn: find the coordinates of four

107
00:05:13.085 --> 00:05:15.747
nine, five in the basis v, s.

108
00:05:15.747 --> 00:05:16.990
Next lecture

109
00:05:16.990 --> 00:05:19.830
the four fundamental subspaces.
